// Tessera stdlib: F128 asinh, acosh, atanh
//
// The inverse hyperbolic functions, correctly rounded (to nearest, ties to even). CORE-MATH has no binary128
// versions, so they run in three tiers:
//
// - quick: below 2^-17 (asinh, atanh) or y = x - 1 below 2^-34 (acosh), a short series in 128-bit fixed point.
//   Elsewhere ln_1p(w) for the w below, with w in fixed point (F128Frac.tess) and the logarithm from CORE-MATH's
//   fast ln path (F128Core/Log.tess) before its rounding. The result is rounded unless it lies too close to a
//   rounding midpoint for its proven error bound. About one random argument in a thousand goes on.
// - fast: the formulas below in F128Extended (192 bits, F128Math.tess). The result is kept when all of it
//   × (1 ± 2^-band) rounds to the same F128 (wide_round_within).
// - exact: otherwise the same formulas in F128Big (448 bits, F128Big.tess), within about 2^-420 relative, rounded
//   once.
//
// On a = |x| (asinh and atanh are odd), with y = x - 1 for acosh:
//
//   asinh a = ln_1p(a + a² / (1 + sqrt(1 + a²)))   (the fast tier uses ln(a + sqrt(a² + 1)) from 1/2 on)
//   acosh x = ln_1p(y + sqrt(y (y + 2)))           (the fast tier uses ln(x + sqrt(x² - 1)) from y = 1/2 on)
//   atanh a = ln_1p(2a / (1 - a)) / 2
//
// None of them cancels: y and 1 - a are exact where it matters, every other sum adds positive terms, and ln_1p
// keeps its relative accuracy near 0, so asinh(2^-16494) and acosh(1 + 2^-112) are as accurate as the rest. Both
// wide types have S64 exponents, so a² can't overflow for a near F128.MAX.
//
// Exact cases: asinh(±0) = ±0, acosh(1) = +0, and atanh(±0) = ±0 (atanh(±1) = ±inf is a pole) are answered first.
// No other input gives an F128 or a midpoint between two, since both are rational: for an algebraic x the results
// are nonzero and e^asinh x = x + sqrt(x² + 1), e^acosh x = x + sqrt(x² - 1), and e^(2 atanh x) = (1 + x) / (1 - x)
// are algebraic, while e^y is transcendental for every nonzero algebraic y (Hermite-Lindemann), so the results are
// transcendental.
//
// The bands are measured, not proven: on 50000 random inputs per function (every exponent from the subnormals to
// F128.MAX, plus runs around the switch points, 1 + tiny for acosh, and 1 - tiny for atanh) the fast tier's worst
// relative error against mpmath was 2^-137.9 for each of the three. That is the log series' first dropped term
// (wide_log stops at t^51 for t = (m - 1) / (m + 1) up to 0.1716, so 2^-138.0 of ln m at m = sqrt(2)), so
// 2^-133 leaves about 5 bits. Random inputs miss the band about once in a million. Results near a rounding
// boundary do occur, where the fast tier alone could round the wrong way: asinh x = x - x³/6 + … and
// atanh x = x + x³/3 + … can be tuned to within 2^-114 ulp of a midpoint for x near 2^-56 (2^-41 ulp near
// 2^-21), and acosh(1 + y) with y = 2k² 2^-112, which is sqrt(2y) = 2k 2^-56 less corrections with small
// denominators, lands within 2^-39 ulp of one for about one k in a thousand (tests/f128_inverse_hyperbolic.tess
// has some of each).
//
// The quick tier's bounds are proven, in units of the result's last bit (a relative 2^-128 to 2^-127):
//
// - Below 2^-58, asinh x and atanh x round to x itself: x³/3 < 2^-117.5 x stays under half an ulp of x (the half
//   ulp below a power of two included, and far under a subnormal's), so the tier returns x.
// - The series (cm_inv_series): asinh a = a (1 - c/6 + 3c²/40 - 15c³/336 + r) and atanh a = a (1 + c/3 + c²/5 +
//   c³/7 + r) with c = a², and acosh(1 + y) = sqrt(2y) (1 - y/12 + 3y²/160 - 5y³/896 + r). The series alternate
//   (atanh's terms shrink by c), so r is below the next term, 35c⁴/1152, c⁴/(9 (1 - c)), and 35y⁴/18432: under
//   2^-139 for a < 2^-17 and y < 2^-34. The polynomial is kept in units of 2^-128: its three divisions floor,
//   and c, c², c³ are cut to whole units, together under 3.7 units. The product with the leading term floors once
//   more (4.7 units of the leading term's last bit), and a borrow shifts the result up a bit, which doubles that
//   (a carry halves it). That is at most (4.7 + 2.01) × 2 = 13.42 units for acosh (its sqrt within 2.01,
//   F128Frac.tess) and 4.7 × 2 = 9.4 for asinh and atanh, so the gates are F128_ACOSH_SERIES_GATE = 14 and
//   F128_INV_SERIES_GATE = 10.
// - The logarithm (cm_inv_ln_1p): w is formed in fixed point within a relative ρ (below), and 1 + w is split
//   exactly into an F128 z (for w < 1, 1 plus the bits of w down to 2^-112, else 1 + w cut to 113 bits) and the
//   rest d = 1 + w - z < 2^-112 z. Then ln(1 + w) = ln z + ln(1 + d/z): ln z from CORE-MATH's fast ln path, which
//   its rounding test takes to be within 13 units of 2^-148 (cm_log_fast), z is outside its window near 1 (w is at
//   least 2^-17), and d/z within 2 units of 2^-148, whose square is far below one more. As ln(1 + w) > 2^-18, its
//   fraction drops at least 3 bits of 2^-148, so these (16 units of 2^-148) are at most 3 units with that
//   truncation. ρ reaches the result as at most ρ w / (1 + w) <= ρ ln(1 + w) for w < 1, and as ρ <= 1.443 ρ
//   ln(1 + w) from w >= 1 on, where 1 + w is cut to 128 bits too (one more 2^-127 in ρ). The worst ρ, in units
//   of 2^-127: asinh's w = a + a²/(1 + sqrt(1 + a²)) below 1 is within 3.4 (its quotient within 4.8, at most half
//   of w) and from a = 1 on z = a + sqrt(a² + 1) within 2.9, acosh's w = y + sqrt(y (y + 2)) within 3.01 and from
//   x = 2 on z = x + sqrt(x² - 1) within 2.68, and atanh's w = 2a / (1 - a) within 3, all one more when 1 + w is
//   cut. The worst is 1.443 × 2 × 4.4 + 3 = 15.7 units, so F128_INV_LOG_GATE = 16.
//
// The gates are bounds rounded up, so the exact result lies on the rounded side of the midpoint (or in the same
// rounding cell at a binade's edge) whenever the guard bits sit farther from it than the gate (cm_frac_round).
// From 2^16380 on, asinh and acosh go on to the fast tier (their z would leave F128's exponent range).

module Standard::Core

preset F128_ASINH_BAND: S64 = 133
preset F128_ACOSH_BAND: S64 = 133
preset F128_ATANH_BAND: S64 = 133

/// The quick tier's gate for the asinh and atanh series, in units of the result's last bit.
/// :note: Proven: the series result is within 9.4 units (the derivation is at the top of this file).
preset F128_INV_SERIES_GATE: U64 = 10

/// The quick tier's gate for the acosh series.
/// :note: Proven: within 13.42 units (the derivation is at the top of this file).
preset F128_ACOSH_SERIES_GATE: U64 = 14

/// The quick tier's gate on the logarithm paths.
/// :note: Proven: within 15.7 units (the derivation is at the top of this file).
preset F128_INV_LOG_GATE: U64 = 16

/// The bits of 2^-58: below it asinh x and atanh x round to x.
preset F128_INV_TINY_BITS: U128 = 0x3FC50000000000000000000000000000

/// The bits of 2^-17: the series below, the logarithm from there on.
preset F128_INV_SERIES_BITS: U128 = 0x3FEE0000000000000000000000000000

/// The bits of 2^16380: from there asinh and acosh skip the quick tier.
preset F128_INV_HUGE_BITS: U128 = 0x7FFB0000000000000000000000000000

// -- quick tier: series and CORE-MATH's fast ln ------------------------------------

/// A finite positive normal F128 as a fraction, exactly.
/// :param u: Its bits.
/// :returns: The same value.
routine cm_inv_frac(u: U128) -> CmFrac
    block entry()
        mantissa : U128   = u.bitand(F128_FRAC_MASK).bitor(F128_IMPLICIT)
        exponent : S64    = f128_exponent(u).sub(16382)
        r        : CmFrac = CmFrac { frac: mantissa.shl(15), exponent: exponent }
        return(r)

/// The series term's polynomial in units of 2^-128: for asinh c/6 - 3c²/40 + 15c³/336, for atanh c/3 + c²/5 +
/// c³/7, and for acosh c/12 - 3c²/160 + 5c³/896, each within 3.7 units.
/// :param c: c × 2^128, below 2^96.
/// :param k: 0 for asinh, 1 for atanh, 2 for acosh.
/// :returns: The polynomial, its value below 2^-33.
routine cm_inv_poly(c: U128, k: U64) -> U128
    shared c2 : U128 = c.mul_wide(c).shr(128).to_wrap<U128>()
    shared c3 : U128 = c2.mul_wide(c).shr(128).to_wrap<U128>()

    block entry()
        when k
            0    -> asinh()
            1    -> atanh()
            else -> acosh()

    block asinh()
        first  : U128 = c.div(6)
        second : U128 = c2.mul(3).div(40)
        third  : U128 = c3.mul(15).div(336)
        r      : U128 = first.sub(second).add(third)
        return(r)

    block atanh()
        first  : U128 = c.div(3)
        second : U128 = c2.div(5)
        third  : U128 = c3.div(7)
        r      : U128 = first.add(second).add(third)
        return(r)

    block acosh()
        first  : U128 = c.div(12)
        second : U128 = c2.mul(3).div(160)
        third  : U128 = c3.mul(5).div(896)
        r      : U128 = first.sub(second).add(third)
        return(r)

/// lead × (1 - p) for asinh and acosh, lead × (1 + p) for atanh, p in units of 2^-128.
/// :param lead: The leading term.
/// :param p: The polynomial from {cm_inv_poly}.
/// :param k: 0 for asinh, 1 for atanh, 2 for acosh.
/// :returns: The series' value.
routine cm_inv_series(lead: CmFrac, p: U128, k: U64) -> CmFrac
    shared product : U128   = lead.frac.mul_wide(p).shr(128).to_wrap<U128>()
    shared term    : CmFrac = cm_frac_normalize(product, lead.exponent)

    block entry()
        grows : Bool = k.eq(1)
        branch grows
            ? return(cm_frac_add(lead, term))
            : return(cm_frac_sub(lead, term))

/// ln(1 + w) for w >= 2^-17 given as a fraction (cut to 113 bits plus the rest, the rest added to CORE-MATH's
/// fast ln of the cut part), within 3 units of ln(1 + w) for the w given.
/// :param w: The argument, at least 2^-17.
/// :returns: ln(1 + w).
routine cm_inv_ln_1p(w: CmFrac) -> CmFrac
    block entry()
        near : Bool = w.exponent.le(0)
        branch near
            ? continue
            : return(cm_inv_ln(cm_frac_add(w, CmFrac { frac: CM_FRAC_TOP, exponent: 1 })))
        // z = 1 + k 2^-112 holds w's bits down to 2^-112, the rest is d = rest × 2^(w.exponent - 128)
        shift : S64  = 16.sub(w.exponent)
        k     : U128 = w.frac.shr(shift.to<U128>())
        rest  : U128 = w.frac.bitand(U128.shl(1, shift.to<U128>()).sub(1))
        bits  : U128 = F128_ONE.bitor(k)
        // d / z × 2^148 = rest × 2^(w.exponent + 83) / (z × 2^63), z × 2^63 cut to 64 bits
        top    : U64    = F128_IMPLICIT.bitor(k).shr(49).to<U64>()
        scaled : U128   = rest.shl(w.exponent.add(83).to<U128>())
        r      : CmFrac = cm_inv_ln_finish(bits, scaled, top)
        return(r)

/// ln z for z >= 2 given as a fraction below 2^16384: ln of z cut to 113 bits from CORE-MATH's fast ln path, plus
/// the rest over the cut part, within 3 units of ln z.
/// :param z: The argument.
/// :returns: ln z.
routine cm_inv_ln(z: CmFrac) -> CmFrac
    block entry()
        rest     : U128 = z.frac.bitand(0x7FFF)
        cut      : U128 = z.frac.sub(rest)
        biased   : U128 = z.exponent.add(16382).to<U128>().shl(112)
        mantissa : U128 = cut.shr(15).bitand(F128_FRAC_MASK)
        // d / z × 2^148 = rest × 2^148 / cut = rest × 2^84 / (cut × 2^-64), cut × 2^-64 cut to 64 bits
        top : U64    = cut.shr(64).to<U64>()
        r   : CmFrac = cm_inv_ln_finish(biased.bitor(mantissa), rest.shl(84), top)
        return(r)

/// ln z plus d/z, for the F128 z with bits `bits` (outside ln's window near 1) and d/z = numer / divisor × 2^-148
/// below 2^-112. The floor of that quotient is within 1 + 2^-25 of d/z in units of 2^-148, as d/z is below 2^37 of
/// them and the divisor is cut by under 2^-63 relative.
/// :param bits: The F128's bits, its logarithm above 2^-18.
/// :param numer: The rest's numerator, below 2^99.
/// :param divisor: z × 2^63 over a power of two, cut to 64 bits, its top bit set.
/// :returns: The sum, its fraction cut at least 3 bits below 2^-148's units.
routine cm_inv_ln_finish(bits: U128, numer: U128, divisor: U64) -> CmFrac
    block entry()
        hi       : U64     = cm_wide_hi(bits)
        e_field  : U64     = hi.bitand(0xFFFF000000000000)
        log      : CmWide3 = cm_log_fast(hi, cm_wide_lo(bits), e_field)
        high     : U64     = numer.shr(64).to<U64>()
        quotient : Div2By1 = div_2by1(high, numer.to_wrap<U64>(), divisor,
            div_2by1_prepare(divisor))
        extra    : U64     = quotient.quotient
        sum      : CmWide3 = cm_wide_add3(log, CmWide3 { w0: extra, w1: 0, w2: 0 })
        // the sum is above 2^130, so its top word holds the leading bit
        shift    : U64    = 64.sub(sum.w2.leading_zeros())
        upper    : U256   = sum.w2.to<U256>().shl(128)
        middle   : U256   = sum.w1.to<U256>().shl(64)
        whole    : U256   = upper.bitor(middle).bitor(sum.w0.to<U256>())
        frac     : U128   = whole.shr(shift.to<U256>()).to_wrap<U128>()
        exponent : S64    = shift.to<S64>().sub(20)
        r        : CmFrac = CmFrac { frac: frac, exponent: exponent }
        return(r)

/// The quick tier of asinh on a > 0 (the derivation is at the top of this file).
/// :param a: The magnitude, finite and nonzero.
/// :returns: The bits of asinh a, correctly rounded.
/// :absent: When the result lies too close to a rounding midpoint, or a >= 2^16380.
routine cm_asinh_quick(a: F128) -> Option<U128>
    shared u   : U128   = a.bits()
    shared one : CmFrac = CmFrac { frac: CM_FRAC_TOP, exponent: 1 }

    block entry()
        tiny   : Bool = u.lt(F128_INV_TINY_BITS)
        series : Bool = u.lt(F128_INV_SERIES_BITS)
        below  : Bool = u.lt(F128_ONE)
        huge   : Bool = u.ge(F128_INV_HUGE_BITS)
        when
            tiny   -> return(.Present(u))
            series -> series()
            below  -> near()
            huge   -> return(.Absent)
            else   -> far()

    block series()
        x : CmFrac       = cm_inv_frac(u)
        c : U128         = x.frac.mul_wide(x.frac).shr(128.sub(x.exponent.mul(2)).to<U256>()).to_wrap<U128>()
        t : CmFrac       = cm_inv_series(x, cm_inv_poly(c, 0), 0)
        r : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, F128_INV_SERIES_GATE)
        return(r)

    // w = a + a² / (1 + sqrt(1 + a²))
    block near()
        x    : CmFrac       = cm_inv_frac(u)
        xx   : CmFrac       = cm_frac_mul(x, x)
        op   : CmFrac       = cm_frac_add(one, xx)
        root : CmFrac       = cm_frac_sqrt(op.frac.to<U256>().shl(128), op.exponent)
        q    : CmFrac       = cm_frac_div(xx, cm_frac_add(root, one))
        t    : CmFrac       = cm_inv_ln_1p(cm_frac_add(x, q))
        r    : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, F128_INV_LOG_GATE)
        return(r)

    // z = a + sqrt(a² + 1)
    block far()
        x    : CmFrac       = cm_inv_frac(u)
        s    : CmFrac       = cm_frac_add(cm_frac_mul(x, x), one)
        root : CmFrac       = cm_frac_sqrt(s.frac.to<U256>().shl(128), s.exponent)
        t    : CmFrac       = cm_inv_ln(cm_frac_add(root, x))
        r    : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, F128_INV_LOG_GATE)
        return(r)

/// The quick tier of acosh on x > 1 (the derivation is at the top of this file).
/// :param x: The argument, finite and above 1.
/// :returns: The bits of acosh x, correctly rounded.
/// :absent: When the result lies too close to a rounding midpoint, or x >= 2^16380.
routine cm_acosh_quick(x: F128) -> Option<U128>
    shared u   : U128   = x.bits()
    shared one : CmFrac = CmFrac { frac: CM_FRAC_TOP, exponent: 1 }
    shared v   : CmFrac = cm_inv_frac(u)

    block entry()
        below_two : Bool = v.exponent.eq(1)
        huge      : Bool = u.ge(F128_INV_HUGE_BITS)
        when
            below_two -> small()
            huge      -> return(.Absent)
            else      -> far()

    // y = x - 1 is exact
    block small()
        y      : CmFrac = cm_frac_normalize(v.frac.sub(CM_FRAC_TOP), 1)
        series : Bool   = y.exponent.lt(-33)
        branch series
            ? series(y)
            : near(y)

    block series(y: CmFrac)
        root : CmFrac       = cm_frac_sqrt(y.frac.to<U256>().shl(128), y.exponent.add(1))
        c    : U128         = y.frac.shr(0.sub(y.exponent).to<U128>())
        t    : CmFrac       = cm_inv_series(root, cm_inv_poly(c, 2), 2)
        r    : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, F128_ACOSH_SERIES_GATE)
        return(r)

    // w = y + sqrt(y (y + 2))
    block near(y: CmFrac)
        two     : CmFrac       = CmFrac { frac: CM_FRAC_TOP, exponent: 2 }
        product : U256         = y.frac.mul_wide(cm_frac_add(two, y).frac)
        root    : CmFrac       = cm_inv_sqrt_product(product, y.exponent.add(2))
        t       : CmFrac       = cm_inv_ln_1p(cm_frac_add(root, y))
        r       : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, F128_INV_LOG_GATE)
        return(r)

    // z = x + sqrt(x² - 1)
    block far()
        s    : CmFrac       = cm_frac_sub(cm_frac_mul(v, v), one)
        root : CmFrac       = cm_frac_sqrt(s.frac.to<U256>().shl(128), s.exponent)
        t    : CmFrac       = cm_inv_ln(cm_frac_add(v, root))
        r    : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, F128_INV_LOG_GATE)
        return(r)

/// sqrt(p × 2^(e - 256)) for a product p of two fractions (p >= 2^254), shifted to set its top bit first.
/// :param p: The product.
/// :param e: The sum of the factors' exponents.
/// :returns: The square root, within 2.01 units.
routine cm_inv_sqrt_product(p: U256, e: S64) -> CmFrac
    block entry()
        top : Bool = p.shr(255).eq(1)
        branch top
            ? return(cm_frac_sqrt(p, e))
            : return(cm_frac_sqrt(p.shl(1), e.sub(1)))

/// The quick tier of atanh on 0 < a < 1 (the derivation is at the top of this file).
/// :param a: The magnitude.
/// :returns: The bits of atanh a, correctly rounded.
/// :absent: When the result lies too close to a rounding midpoint.
routine cm_atanh_quick(a: F128) -> Option<U128>
    shared u   : U128   = a.bits()
    shared one : CmFrac = CmFrac { frac: CM_FRAC_TOP, exponent: 1 }

    block entry()
        tiny   : Bool = u.lt(F128_INV_TINY_BITS)
        series : Bool = u.lt(F128_INV_SERIES_BITS)
        when
            tiny   -> return(.Present(u))
            series -> series()
            else   -> logarithm()

    block series()
        x : CmFrac       = cm_inv_frac(u)
        c : U128         = x.frac.mul_wide(x.frac).shr(128.sub(x.exponent.mul(2)).to<U256>()).to_wrap<U128>()
        t : CmFrac       = cm_inv_series(x, cm_inv_poly(c, 1), 1)
        r : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, F128_INV_SERIES_GATE)
        return(r)

    // w = 2a / (1 - a): 1 - a is exact from 1/2 on, else within a unit
    block logarithm()
        x        : CmFrac = cm_inv_frac(u)
        upper    : Bool   = x.exponent.eq(0)
        exact    : CmFrac = cm_frac_normalize(0.sub_wrap(x.frac), 0)
        computed : CmFrac = cm_frac_sub(one, x)
        gap      : CmFrac = upper
            ? exact
            : computed
        twice : CmFrac       = CmFrac { frac: x.frac, exponent: x.exponent.add(1) }
        t     : CmFrac       = cm_inv_ln_1p(cm_frac_div(twice, gap))
        r     : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent.sub(1), 0, F128_INV_LOG_GATE)
        return(r)

// -- fast tier: F128Extended ---------------------------------------------------

/// asinh a for a > 0: ln_1p(a + a²/(1 + sqrt(a² + 1))) below 1/2, else ln(a + sqrt(a² + 1)).
/// :param a: The argument, positive.
/// :returns: asinh a at 192 bits.
routine wide_asinh(a: F128Extended) -> F128Extended
    shared aa   : F128Extended = a.mul(a)
    shared root : F128Extended = aa.add(wide_one()).sqrt()

    block entry()
        small : Bool = a.exponent.lt(-1)
        branch small
            ? near()
            : return(wide_log(a.add(root)))

    block near()
        r : F128Extended = wide_ln_1p(a.add(aa.div(wide_one().add(root))))
        return(r)

/// acosh x for x > 1. Here y = x - 1 is exact wherever it's used (below 1/2).
/// :param x: The argument, above 1.
/// :returns: acosh x at 192 bits.
routine wide_acosh(x: F128) -> F128Extended
    shared w : F128Extended = x.to<F128Extended>()
    shared y : F128Extended = w.sub(wide_one())

    block entry()
        small : Bool = y.exponent.lt(-1)
        branch small
            ? near()
            : far()

    block near()
        root : F128Extended = y.mul(y.add(S64.to<F128Extended>(2))).sqrt()
        r    : F128Extended = wide_ln_1p(y.add(root))
        return(r)

    block far()
        radicand : F128Extended = w.mul(w).sub(wide_one())
        root     : F128Extended = radicand.sqrt()
        r        : F128Extended = wide_log(w.add(root))
        return(r)

/// atanh a for 0 < a < 1, as ln_1p(2a / (1 - a)) / 2.
/// :param a: The argument.
/// :returns: atanh a at 192 bits.
routine wide_atanh(a: F128) -> F128Extended
    block entry()
        w   : F128Extended = a.to<F128Extended>()
        arg : F128Extended = w.ldexp(1).div(wide_one().sub(w))
        r   : F128Extended = wide_ln_1p(arg).ldexp(-1)
        return(r)

// -- exact tier: F128Big -------------------------------------------------------

/// asinh a for a > 0, as ln_1p(a + a²/(1 + sqrt(a² + 1))).
/// :param a: The argument, positive.
/// :returns: asinh a at 448 bits.
routine big_asinh(a: F128) -> F128Big
    block entry()
        b    : F128Big = a.to<F128Big>()
        one  : F128Big = big_one()
        bb   : F128Big = b.mul(b)
        root : F128Big = bb.add(one).sqrt()
        r    : F128Big = big_ln_1p(b.add(bb.div(one.add(root))))
        return(r)

/// acosh x for x > 1, as ln_1p(y + sqrt(y (y + 2))) with y = x - 1.
/// :param x: The argument, above 1.
/// :returns: acosh x at 448 bits.
routine big_acosh(x: F128) -> F128Big
    block entry()
        y    : F128Big = x.to<F128Big>().sub(big_one())
        root : F128Big = y.mul(y.add(S64.to<F128Big>(2))).sqrt()
        r    : F128Big = big_ln_1p(y.add(root))
        return(r)

/// atanh a for 0 < a < 1, as ln_1p(2a / (1 - a)) / 2.
/// :param a: The argument.
/// :returns: atanh a at 448 bits.
routine big_atanh(a: F128) -> F128Big
    block entry()
        b   : F128Big = a.to<F128Big>()
        arg : F128Big = b.ldexp(1).div(big_one().sub(b))
        r   : F128Big = big_ln_1p(arg).ldexp(-1)
        return(r)

// -- asinh, acosh, atanh -------------------------------------------------------

/// asinh, correctly rounded: ±0 and ±inf are their own, and a NaN comes back quieted.
/// :returns: asinh(`self`).
routine F128.asinh(self: Self) -> Self
    block entry()
        r : Self = f128_asinh(self, false)
        return(r)

/// acosh, correctly rounded: +0 at 1, +inf at +inf, NaN below 1, and a NaN comes back quieted.
/// :returns: acosh(`self`).
routine F128.acosh(self: Self) -> Self
    block entry()
        r : Self = f128_acosh(self, false)
        return(r)

/// atanh, correctly rounded: ±0 at ±0, ±inf at ±1, NaN beyond, and a NaN comes back quieted.
/// :returns: atanh(`self`).
routine F128.atanh(self: Self) -> Self
    block entry()
        r : Self = f128_atanh(self, false)
        return(r)

/// asinh x, correctly rounded, as {F128.asinh}.
/// :param x: The argument.
/// :param exact: True skips the quick and fast tiers (the tests use it to check the exact tier on its own).
/// :returns: asinh x.
routine f128_asinh(x: F128, exact: Bool) -> F128
    block entry()
        bits : U128 = x.bits()
        nan  : Bool = f128_is_nan_bits(bits)
        zero : Bool = f128_is_zero_bits(bits)
        inf  : Bool = x.is_infinite()
        when
            nan  -> return(f128_of(f128_quiet(bits)))
            zero -> return(x)
            inf  -> return(x)
            else -> tiers(x.abs())

    block tiers(a: F128)
        branch exact
            ? slow(a)
            : continue
        q : Option<U128> = cm_asinh_quick(a)
        when q
            .Present(found) -> return(f128_of(found).copysign(x))
            .Absent         -> continue
        w       : F128Extended = wide_asinh(a.to<F128Extended>())
        rounded : WideRounding = wide_round_within(w, F128_ASINH_BAND)
        branch rounded.ok
            ? return(rounded.value.copysign(x))
            : slow(a)

    block slow(a: F128)
        magnitude : F128 = big_asinh(a).to<F128>()
        r         : F128 = magnitude.copysign(x)
        return(r)

/// acosh x, correctly rounded, as {F128.acosh}.
/// :param x: The argument.
/// :param exact: True skips the quick and fast tiers.
/// :returns: acosh x.
routine f128_acosh(x: F128, exact: Bool) -> F128
    block entry()
        bits  : U128 = x.bits()
        nan   : Bool = f128_is_nan_bits(bits)
        one   : F128 = f128_of(F128_ONE)
        below : Bool = x.lt(one)
        unit  : Bool = x.eq(one)
        inf   : Bool = x.is_infinite()
        when
            nan   -> return(f128_of(f128_quiet(bits)))
            below -> return(F128.NAN)
            unit  -> return(f128_of(0))
            inf   -> return(x)
            else  -> tiers()

    block tiers()
        branch exact
            ? slow()
            : continue
        q : Option<U128> = cm_acosh_quick(x)
        when q
            .Present(found) -> return(f128_of(found))
            .Absent         -> continue
        rounded : WideRounding = wide_round_within(wide_acosh(x), F128_ACOSH_BAND)
        branch rounded.ok
            ? return(rounded.value)
            : slow()

    block slow()
        r : F128 = big_acosh(x).to<F128>()
        return(r)

/// atanh x, correctly rounded, as {F128.atanh}.
/// :param x: The argument.
/// :param exact: True skips the quick and fast tiers.
/// :returns: atanh x.
routine f128_atanh(x: F128, exact: Bool) -> F128
    shared bits : U128 = x.bits()
    shared nan  : Bool = f128_is_nan_bits(bits)
    shared zero : Bool = f128_is_zero_bits(bits)
    shared a    : F128 = x.abs()

    block entry()
        one    : F128 = f128_of(F128_ONE)
        at_one : Bool = a.eq(one)
        beyond : Bool = a.gt(one)
        when
            nan    -> return(f128_of(f128_quiet(bits)))
            zero   -> return(x)
            beyond -> return(F128.NAN)
            at_one -> return(F128.INFINITY.copysign(x))
            else   -> tiers()

    block tiers()
        branch exact
            ? slow()
            : continue
        q : Option<U128> = cm_atanh_quick(a)
        when q
            .Present(found) -> return(f128_of(found).copysign(x))
            .Absent         -> continue
        rounded : WideRounding = wide_round_within(wide_atanh(a), F128_ATANH_BAND)
        branch rounded.ok
            ? return(rounded.value.copysign(x))
            : slow()

    block slow()
        magnitude : F128 = big_atanh(a).to<F128>()
        r         : F128 = magnitude.copysign(x)
        return(r)
